<title>UK: Schroders H1 pretax profit hits record.</title>
<headline>Schroders H1 pretax profit hits record.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			  (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		  46.3		 vs 29.7</p>
<p> Dividend  (pence)	  6.0		  vs 4.5</p>
<p> Pretax			 115.9		vs 85.6</p>
<p> Operating income	   462.4		vs 355.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits for UK-based investment bank Schroders Plc were in a range of 106-125 million stg. A dividend of 5.0-6.0 pence per share was expected.  </p>
<p> Tax			    23.2		 vs 25.8</p>
<p> Net taxed		    92.7		 vs 59.8</p>
<p> Net interest income	59.7		 vs 58.8</p>
<p> Operating expenses	 336.2		vs 266.8</p>
<p> Attributable		 90.3		 vs 57.8</p>
<p> Pay date		     October 24</p>
<p> Div registration date    September 24</p>
<p> Ex-div date		  September 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Investment bank Schroders Plc said in the six months ending June 30, 1996 it had a net increase in provisions for sales aid leasing of 1.6 million stg and recoveries in the sector of 0.4 million stg.</p>
<p>In banking, it had no net decrease in provisions and recoveries of 0.2 million stg.</p>
<p>The net provision for bad debt in the period was one million stg, the bank said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
